    STEP A-3.18 fixup: T5 skip under sanitizer → TSan exit 0
    
    Per Steward A-3.18 directive: "TSan: exit 0 with no data races" and
    "Separate the T5 oversized-allocation limitation from other test results."
    
    Root cause of TSAN_EXIT=66 in prior A-3.18 run: T5 calls calloc(huge, 3)
    which TSan intercepts and rejects as "allocation-size-too-big" BEFORE the
    profiler sees it, causing the process to abort. This prevented T6-T10 from
    running under TSan and produced exit 66.
    
    FIX: T5 now calls SKIP_IF_DISABLED() at the top. When a sanitizer is
    detected (profiler self-disables under TSan/ASan), T5 is skipped entirely.
    This achieves the separation Steward requested: T5's overflow tests run in
    the plain suite (verifying the profiler's guards), while TSan focuses on
    concurrency (T8/T9/T10) without being aborted by oversized allocations.
    
    Updated test script acceptance criteria:
      - TSAN_EXIT must now be 0 (was: accepted non-zero with size-abort excuse)
      - TSAN_SIZE_ABORT must now be 0 (was: accepted >= 1)
    
    Results after fix:
      Plain suite  : 81 tests, exit 0
      TSan         : exit 0, 0 data races, 0 size aborts
      Node smoke   : exit 0
      PROD isolation: verified
    
    ALL CHECKS PASSED (including TSan exit 0).

